answer('1.2:eip-302',ol('Honor students alone likely overestimate the all-student GPA. Use a random sample across all students.','Every twentieth eligible child is systematic sampling, but one store and one time window may omit important groups. Broaden locations and times.','Representatives’ incomes do not represent all U.S. adults. Selecting states and then all representatives is cluster sampling within the wrong population; it does not repair the mismatch.','The bench sample is convenience sampling from one city and is unlikely to represent the intended commuter population.','A simple random sample of hospitals across the state is a reasonable starting point for the mean across hospitals. A mean across patient stays would require appropriate patient/stay weighting.'))
