answer('Try It 1.20','Explanatory variable: active pill versus placebo. Response: change in test-completion time from before to after treatment. Treatments are the headache-inducing pill and the inactive look-alike. Possible other influences include baseline ability, fatigue, expectations, and practice with the test. Random assignment helps balance them. Participants and outcome evaluators can be blinded, though noticeable symptoms may partially reveal treatment.')
