answer('Example 2.15','There are 50 observations. The 14th is 6 and the 15th is 7, so the textbook’s 28th-percentile result is (6 + 7)/2 = 6.5 hours. The 25th and 26th values are both 7, giving median 7. The third quartile is 8. Repeated values mean it is incorrect to insist that exactly 75% of observations are strictly below Q₃; here only 52% are strictly below 8, and 80% are at or below 8.')
