answer('Try It 2.16','Use the section’s stated rule i = (k/100)(n + 1); an integer picks that position and a noninteger averages the two adjacent positions. For n = 29, i₂₀ = 6, so P₂₀ = 27. For P₅₅, i = 16.5, so average positions 16 and 17: (52 + 55)/2 = 53.5 years. Other percentile conventions may give different results.')
answer('Try It 2.17','Q₃ = 4 hours. It is also called the 75th percentile. The first 26 observations are 2 or 3 hours; positions 27–36 are all 4 hours.')
